$DIR/main.p:21:27: cannot return readAll(2).Slice(), which points into the temporary Buf that readAll(2) returns
    readAll(2).Slice() points into the temporary Buf that readAll(2) returns.
    The Buf that readAll(2) returns (at main.p:21) is a temporary: nothing keeps
    it, so it is the receiver of the method only until the end of the statement.
    A view of it may be passed to calls in that statement but may not outlive
    it. At the end of the statement, the temporary is dropped, before the caller
    gets readAll(2).Slice(), so it would point at a value that has been dropped.
    The view does not own the memory it looks at. Nothing keeps the temporary
    after the statement, so a stored view would outlive the value that keeps its
    memory alive.
    Return the Buf itself, which keeps its memory alive in the caller, or a copy
    of what the view looks at.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3009" for a longer explanation)
